<main class="content settings-page">
  <div class="settings-head">
    <div>
      <span class="settings-kicker">CHILD SAFETY STANDARDS</span>
      <h1>Lumi Child Safety Standards</h1>
      <p class="muted">Standards against child sexual abuse and exploitation (CSAE) · Updated September 14, 2026</p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn ghost" href="/terms">Terms of Use</a>
  </div>

  <section class="card settings-card">
    <h2>1. Zero tolerance for CSAE</h2>
    <p>Lumi has zero tolerance for child sexual abuse and exploitation (CSAE). Users must not create, upload, share, solicit, promote, facilitate, or distribute content or behavior that sexually exploits, abuses, or endangers a child. This includes grooming for sexual exploitation, sextortion, trafficking of a child for sexual purposes, and any other form of child sexual exploitation or abuse.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card settings-card">
    <h2>2. Child sexual abuse material (CSAM)</h2>
    <p>Child sexual abuse material (CSAM) is strictly prohibited on Lumi. This includes visual depictions such as photos, videos, computer-generated imagery, or other media involving minors in sexually explicit conduct. Content suspected to be CSAM may be removed or disabled immediately, and accounts involved may be suspended or permanently terminated.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card settings-card">
    <h2>3. In-app reporting</h2>
    <p>Lumi provides in-app reporting tools for user-generated content. Users can use the Report action available on posts and other supported content to flag safety concerns. Reports are reviewed and may result in content removal, visibility restrictions, account restrictions, suspension, or permanent termination.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card settings-card">
    <h2>4. Enforcement and response</h2>
    <p>When Lumi identifies or receives a credible report of content or behavior involving CSAE or CSAM, we may preserve relevant information as required by law, restrict access to the content, remove it, disable the responsible account, and take other appropriate safety actions. Where required by applicable law, Lumi will cooperate with and report to relevant regional or national authorities.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card settings-card">
    <h2>5. Child safety laws</h2>
    <p>Lumi is intended for users aged 18 and over. Regardless of age gating, Lumi complies with applicable child safety laws and prohibits child sexual abuse and exploitation across the service.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card settings-card">
    <h2>6. Child safety contact</h2>
    <p>For child safety concerns, policy questions, or urgent reports related to CSAE/CSAM, contact Lumi at <a href="mailto:hallaymstore@gmail.com">hallaymstore@gmail.com</a>. If a child is in immediate danger, contact local law enforcement or an appropriate child-safety organization in your country.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card settings-card">
    <h2>7. O‘zbekistoncha qisqacha</h2>
    <p>Lumi bolalarga nisbatan jinsiy zo‘ravonlik va ekspluatatsiya (CSAE), shuningdek CSAM materiallariga nisbatan qat’iy nol toqat siyosatini qo‘llaydi. Bunday kontentni yaratish, yuklash, tarqatish, so‘rash yoki targ‘ib qilish taqiqlanadi. Foydalanuvchilar ilova ichidagi Report funksiyasi orqali shubhali kontent haqida xabar berishi mumkin. Qoidabuzar kontent o‘chirilishi, akkaunt cheklanishi yoki bloklanishi va qonun talab qilgan hollarda tegishli organlarga xabar berilishi mumkin.</p>
  </section>
</main>
